    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "#| label: ex5-simulate-returns\n",
        "\n",
        "def simulate_returns(periods, expected_returns, covariance_matrix):\n",
        "    returns = np.random.multivariate_normal(\n",
        "        expected_returns,\n",
        "        covariance_matrix,\n",
        "        size=periods\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return returns"
      ],
      "id": "ex5-simulate-returns",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Using this function, we repeatedly simulate returns (15 times) and construct plug-in efficient frontiers based on the estimated parameters $\\hat{\\mu}$ and $\\hat{\\Sigma}$. We consider sample sizes of $T=60$, $T=120$ and $T=500$ to examine how the magnitude of estimation error depends on the amount of available data."
      ],
